# {{name}} - Agent Sandbox Template

This is an E2B sandbox template that allows you to run code in a controlled environment.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have:
- An Alibaba Agent Sandbox account
- A sandbox API key from the Alibaba Console
{{#if isTypeScript}}- Node.js and npm/yarn (or similar) installed{{else if isPython}}- Python installed{{/if}}

## Configuration

1. Create a `.env` file in your project root or set the environment variable:
   ```
   {{#if isPython}}ABX_SANDBOX_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
   ABX_SANDBOX_BASE_URL=https://api.<region>.sandbox.aliyuncs.com
   ABX_SANDBOX_DOMAIN=<region>.sandbox.aliyuncs.com{{else}}E2B_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
   E2B_API_URL=https://api.<region>.sandbox.aliyuncs.com
   E2B_DOMAIN=<region>.sandbox.aliyuncs.com{{/if}}
   ```

## Installing Dependencies

```bash
{{#if isTypeScript}}
npm install e2b
{{else if isPython}}
python -m pip install --index-url https://pypi.org/simple "agent-sandbox-client==0.4.0a6"
{{/if}}
```

## Building the Template

```bash
{{#if isTypeScript}}
# For development
npm run e2b:build:dev

# For production
npm run e2b:build:prod
{{else if isPython}}
# For development
make e2b:build:dev

# For production
make e2b:build:prod
{{/if}}
```

## Using the Template in a Sandbox

Once your template is built, you can use it in your E2B sandbox:

{{#if isTypeScript}}
```typescript
import { Sandbox } from 'e2b'

// Create a new sandbox instance
const sandbox = await Sandbox.create('{{name}}')

// Your sandbox is ready to use!
console.log('Sandbox created successfully')
```
{{else if isPythonSync}}
```python
from agent_sandbox import Sandbox

# Create a new sandbox instance
sandbox = Sandbox.create('{{name}}')
try:
    print('Sandbox created successfully')
finally:
    sandbox.kill()
```
{{else if isPythonAsync}}
```python
from agent_sandbox import AsyncSandbox
import asyncio

async def main():
    # Create a new sandbox instance
    sandbox = await AsyncSandbox.create('{{name}}')
    try:
        print('Sandbox created successfully')
    finally:
        await sandbox.kill()

# Run the async function
asyncio.run(main())
```
{{/if}}

## Template Structure

- `{{templateFile}}` - Defines the sandbox template configuration
- `{{buildDevFile}}` - Builds the template for development
- `{{buildProdFile}}` - Builds the template for production

